# Based off Canadian cement production in 1977 vs. 2000 (and employment in the construction industry in the respective years), there are roughly ~13.4t/worker/year in 1977 vs ~14.9 in 2000. 
# We will scale cement consumption accordingly for 1960 vs 1985 builders' yards.
# 13.4/14.9 * 50 = 45
# We use this, alongside the employment_capacity, to scale the productivity: 100 * 45/50 * 70/125 = 50
# Basically we keep the ratios the same here but overall productivity is halved.
