upgrade[0]=BuildersYard1985

--------------------
# Assumption 1: Based off this quora post (https://www.quora.com/How-many-construction-workers-are-needed-to-build-a-22-000-sq-ft-museum-in-1-2-years), a 22,000 sq.ft building requires around 150-250 workers to build it. 
# Ingame builders' yards are 1x2 tiles, which comes out to 336,000 sq.ft, which comes out to ~3,000 workers per builders' yard. We will not deal with floor area ratios as these numbers are hard to find, so we will assume an average FAR of ~1.0.
# Also we will probably not go for a 3,000-worker builders' yard, just because that would be impractical to actually staff in-game.
# Based off taking amounts consumed by the UK construction industry (the entirety of cement and brick production, ~50% of steel production, and 5M tonnes/year direct quote for softwood timber), we divide those amounts by 2016 UK construction industry employment (1.35M employees).
# This gets us, for a modern builders' yard:
# 99.7t of concrete
# 12.9t of planks
# 35.3 crates of bricks
# 48.62t of steel
# Since these numbers are ROUGHLY compatible with the production figures for associated industries, we'll go with them, and scale these proportionally backwards.
